ENTRY            C3129   20260514   20260819   20260819       C258
SUBENT        C3129001   20260514   20260819   20260819       C258
BIB                 11         29
TITLE      Study of the Be(p,n) and Be(d,n) Source Reactions
AUTHOR     (T.N.Massey,D.K.Jacobs,S.I.Al-Quraishi,S.M.Grimes,
           C.E.Brient,W.B.Howard,J.C.Yanch,T.W.Covell,D.L.Smith,
           B.J.Micklich,Y.Xu,G.Garty,S.A.Marino,G.Randers-Pehrson,
           G.W.Johnson,D.J.Brenner)
REFERENCE  (J,NST,39,677,2002) Main reference: 3,7 MeV data.
           #doi:10.1080/00223131.2002.10875190
           (J,FED,37,57,1997) Preliminary results: 3,7 MeV data.
           #doi:10.1016/S0920-3796(97)00031-8
           (J,JINS,7,C03031,2012) 5 MeV data.
           #doi:10.1088/1748-0221/7/03/C03031
INSTITUTE  (1USAOHO,1USAMIT,1USAANL,1USACOL)
FACILITY   (VDGT,1USAOHO) The T11 tandem Van de Graaff, and TOF
           tunnel of the Ohio University Accelerator Laboratory.
DETECTOR   (GLASD,SCIN) Four to six lithium-loaded glass
           scintillators. A detector array made up of seven
           11.5-cm diameter x 5 cm thick NE213 scintillators.
SAMPLE     The targets used were 2.5 cm square, and 0.25 and 0.5
           mm thick, and 99.9% pure in their beryllium content.
METHOD     (TOF) Standard TOF techniques were used in the
           determination of neutron spectra.
ERR-ANALYS (ERR-S) Statistical errors.
           (ERR-1) There is an additional 5% error in the
           absolute normalization of the Al(d,n) spectra from
           the uncertainty in the composition of the fission
           foils used to determine the Al(d,n) spectrum at 7.44
           MeV and 120 degrees.
STATUS     (APRVD) Approved by Dr. Th.Massey on May 21, 2026.
HISTORY    (20260514C) BP
ENDBIB              29
COMMON               1          3
ERR-1
PER-CENT
        5.0
ENDCOMMON            3
